-- title:
--   H²(D_w,K_w^×) is generated by the transported fundamental class
-- statement:
--   Let $E\subseteq K$ be number fields with $K/E$ Galois, let $w$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$, and write $D_w$ for [`NumberField.PlaceDecomp.decomp E K w`](def/NumberField_PlaceDecompositionAction.html#L82), the decomposition subgroup of the valuation subring of the $w$-adic valuation of $K$ inside $K\simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[E]}K$; assume $D_w$ is solvable. Let $q$ be a prime and $L$ a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ inside a fixed algebraic closure, carrying an action of $D_w$ by ring automorphisms together with a compatible action on $L^\times$, and let $\Phi\colon K_w\to L$ be a ring isomorphism of the $w$-adic completion with $L$. The hypotheses require that $D_w$ fix $\mathbb{Q}_q$ pointwise in $L$, that the unit action be the restriction of the action on $L$, and that $\Phi$ be $D_w$-equivariant. Let $K_0$ be a further finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ which is a base for $L$ under $D_w$, i.e. $K_0\le L$ and an element of $L$ lies in $K_0$ exactly when it is fixed by all of $D_w$. Let $\theta$ be a morphism of $\mathbb{Z}[D_w]$-representations from $L^\times$ (written additively) to $K_w^\times$ whose underlying map is $\Phi^{-1}$ on unit groups, and let $u\in H^2(D_w,L^\times)$ satisfy `IsLocalFundamentalClass`, the requirement that for every finite overlayer $M\supseteq L$ with finite group $H$, normal subgroups $N_L,N_n$, isomorphism $D_w\cong H/N_L$, Frobenius element $\varphi$ and uniformiser $\pi$ forming an unramified overlayer datum over $K_0$, and every unit-compatible comparison morphism $\iota$, the image of $u$ in $H^2(H,M^\times)$ is the inflation of the class of the cyclic carry cocycle built from $\varphi$ and $\pi$. Then every $z\in H^2(D_w,K_w^\times)$ satisfies $z=m\cdot(\theta_*u)$ for some $m\in\mathbb{Z}$, where $\theta_*$ is the map on $H^2$ induced by $\theta$ over the identity of $D_w$.
--
--   This is the local class formation statement that $H^2$ of the decomposition group acting on the local field's unit group is cyclic, generated by the fundamental class, in the form needed downstream: every class has an integer "local reading". It supplies the integers used by the reciprocity-law bookkeeping for idèle classes (inflation, restriction and corestriction of local invariants, and the cyclic and $p$-group layers of the Herbrand-quotient argument).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_NumberField_PlaceDecomp_exists_eq_zsmul_map_of_isLocalFundamentalClass.lean

